# Security and Privacy

NextCue handles ADHD-related, psychological, task, and behavior data. Treat leaks as **Critical**.

## Auth and ownership

1. Backend must verify Clerk JWT on protected routes.
2. `user_id` for authorization comes only from the verified token.
3. Never authorize using client-supplied `user_id` alone.
4. Every task (and similar resource) query/mutation must check ownership.
5. Frontend must not store sensitive secrets (no long-lived raw tokens in localStorage as a design).

## Product and clinical boundaries

1. Do not describe NextCue as medical diagnosis or treatment.
2. Do not make clinical judgments from Onboarding answers.
3. Onboarding answers used for personalization must be explicitly documented; unused answers must not drive hidden “diagnosis”.

## Data handling

1. Do not log full chat transcripts, tokens, or sensitive PII.
2. AI prompts send the minimum data needed for the feature.
3. Third-party AI Providers must not receive unrelated identity fields.
4. Never use real user data as development Mock.
5. Tests use separate test accounts and test databases.
6. Users must be able to delete account and personal data (implement when product phase reaches it; design must not block it).
7. Production writes only through official business APIs.

## Diagnosis / audit ban

Do not probe other users’ IDs to “prove” a leak. Document missing auth gates without expanding blast radius.
